dist
coverage
.DS_Store
*.log

# Every .env variant, not just .env, because the file that gets committed by
# accident is never the one called .env: it is .env.local or .env.production.bak,
# made in a hurry on the day something is broken. .env.example is the exception and
# has to stay tracked, since `cp .env.example .env` is the first line of the README.
.env*
!.env.example
